  "brief_rationale": "The doctor immediately recognized new chest pain as the priority (RC1) and escalated to emergency (RC3, RC4) without attributing it to anxiety. However, targeted current-status assessment (RC2) was never performed—no explicit questions about onset/duration, radiation detail, associated symptoms beyond what the family volunteered—despite multiple opportunities. This omission is a minor-to-moderate responsibility-chain error that caps the grade at 2. No high-order point was validly completed with trajectory impact because the model never corrected a named family misconception, never actively reconciled hidden medication-order structure, and never maintained dynamic reprioritization across the family’s repeated pullbacks. The closure is safe and receives adequate teach-back, but the RC2 gap is decisive.",
